WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.610
Zoe Saldana's convincing turn as the green-skinned
alien assassin Gamora made her an immediate

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.300
fan favorite in the Guardians of the Galaxy
franchise.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.580
And the adopted daughter of Thanos plays a
key role in the massive superhero crossover

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.090
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:18.560
It takes a lot of work to transform Saldana
from All-American actress to otherworldly

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.530
badass, and it begins well before she ever
sits down in the makeup chair.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.289
The Gamora regimen

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:28.101
There's always a certain amount of physical
preparation involved for a major role in a

00:00:28.101 --> 00:00:32.119
Marvel film, but to reprise her role as Gamora
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2, Saldana

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:35.030
had to go a little above and beyond.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:40.090
In November 2014, the actress gave birth to
twins — and subsequently dropped 70 pounds

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.699
after embarking on an exercise regimen that
would make Drax cry.

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:47.879
She had difficulty bouncing back at first,
starting off with simply taking walks, and

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:52.899
eventually working up to a brutal routine
of squats, planks, lunges and Pilates combined

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:54.309
with regular cardio.

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:58.850
Although she's 80 percent gluten-free and
leans heavily on eggs, vegetables and greens,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.280
she insists she doesn't follow a strict diet.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.420
As she put it in a 2015 Facebook post,

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.790
"I am going to remove the word 'diet' from
my life.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:10.180
I am going to remind myself that it is not
about losing weight, it is about being healthy,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.860
feeling healthy, for the rest of my life."

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.860
Head on

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.390
Saldana famously played another colorful alien
in 2009's Avatar, but in that case, she got

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.410
off easy, since her entire character was digitally
rendered.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:26.640
So it may have come as a bit of a surprise
to Saldana the first time the makeup department

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.480
working on Guardians of the Galaxy told her
that they'd need to make a full cast of her

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.480
head.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.200
The procedure looks pretty grueling, especially
if you're claustrophobic.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.780
No CGI required

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.640
The head-cast allows effects artists exercise
great attention to detail when designing Gamora's

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.880
facial "appliances" and makeup.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.350
This is necessary because, in contrast with
her Avatar role, there are exactly zero computer

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.909
generated elements to Gamora.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:54.060
According to Guardians 2 makeup designer David
White, prosthetics made from silicone are

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.100
sculpted for her cheeks and forehead, the
latter of which gives her a new brow line.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.800
The pieces take two to three hours to apply,
and about 30 to 45 minutes to remove.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:07.090
Her prosthetic forehead actually has a "scalp"
piece that runs underneath her wig — that's

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.810
right, she also has to wear a wig — so that
even the edge of her hairline and her part

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.810
line are green.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.560
Of course, the prosthetics are only the beginning.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.880
Five hour job

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.220
As with any paint job, Saldana gets multiple
complete coats of primer before makeup artists

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.829
get down to the business of greening her up
completely.

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:27.870
A green base comes after the primer, followed
by three more layers which are airbrushed

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.870
on.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.069
This is done to get as close possible to a
natural tone.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.140
It all meant a grueling five hours in the
makeup chair for the first Guardians film,

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.610
but only four hours for the follow-up…

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:41.730
"We shaved off an hour from the first movie,
so I appreciate that, um ..."

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.730
Label check

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.959
Surprisingly, virtually all of the brands
used to turn Saldana into Gamora are mainstream,

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:49.519
commercially available products.

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:53.689
White and his team seem to be particularly
fond of M.A.C., a popular brand that's used

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:58.049
for both the initial layer of primer and for
the green base that's applied before the airbrushing

00:02:58.049 --> 00:02:59.049
begins.

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:03.200
Products from Skin Illustrator and Aqua are
used for the airbrush job, and her eyeshadow

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.510
is a careful blend of several M.A.C. products.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.659
Her nail polish is from Sinful Colours, and
her green lipstick is from high-end brand

00:03:09.659 --> 00:03:11.400
Kryolan.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.120
Not easy being green

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.730
Of course, it took a great deal of time and
consideration to arrive at the right shade

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.749
of green for a character that would also be
spending a lot of time in front of green and

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:21.749
blue screens.

00:03:21.749 --> 00:03:25.849
White and his team needed tons of tests to
nail down the right tone, and then were tasked

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:30.169
with using their array of products to faithfully
recreate that exact tone day after day for

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:34.799
the duration of the shoot — one he describes
as "multilayered" with at least three complementary

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:38.489
tones running through it, in addition to Saldana's
natural skin tone.

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:42.769
If it all seems like a lot of trouble, well,
it is — but if Marvel Studios wants us to

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:46.749
believe that a raccoon can talk, then it's
certainly not about to cut corners to convince

00:03:46.749 --> 00:03:49.359
us that a stunning alien assassin can be green.

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:50.359
Thanks for watching!

